WEBVTT

00:05:29.408 --> 00:05:32.536
Many startups disappear fairly quickly
after being founded.

00:05:33.621 --> 00:05:35.039
And it’s very, very tempting,

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:37.500
given all of your experience
in the business,

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:38.501
to judge them.

00:05:39.585 --> 00:05:41.128
Do they know what they’re doing?

00:05:41.128 --> 00:05:42.922
Does their business model make sense?

00:05:42.922 --> 00:05:44.382
Will they ever make any money?

00:05:44.799 --> 00:05:47.676
But instead of judging them
from the comfort

00:05:47.676 --> 00:05:49.678
and the confidence of your position,

00:05:49.678 --> 00:05:53.766
try assuming that it’s they that have
the right bet on the future.

00:05:55.226 --> 00:05:58.104
Think about the consequences
of that for your business model.

00:05:58.479 --> 00:06:01.607
Try making the best case for their idea.